-> A particle type is just a named schema, built from the predefined
-> `Particle` base (`_class`/`_created`) and `∩` (schema merge) — no
-> separate `type` keyword. `_class` is pinned explicitly to the name.
-> Constructing a value validates it against that schema.
Point = Particle ∩ { _class ∈ "Point", x ∈ Number, y ∈ Number }
origin = Point { x = 0, y = 0 }
assert origin.x = 0

-> Union types: a value satisfying *either* side.
id = 42
assert id ∈ Number ∪ String

-> Intersection types: a value satisfying *both* sides.
n = 7
assert n ∈ Number ∩ Number
